    <string name="onion_description">A versatile bulb vegetable, essential in many dishes. Easy to grow in containers.</string>
    <string name="garlic_description">A pungent bulb vegetable, known for its health benefits and strong flavor.</string>
    <string name="cucumber_description">A refreshing vine vegetable, perfect for salads and pickling.</string>
    <string name="tomato_description">A juicy fruit-vegetable, rich in vitamins and perfect for sauces and salads.</string>
    <string name="carrot_description">A crunchy root vegetable, rich in beta-carotene and great for health.</string>

    <string name="onion_guide_title">🌱 Onion Growing Guide</string>
    <string name="garlic_guide_title">🌱 Garlic Growing Guide</string>
    <string name="cucumber_guide_title">🌱 Cucumber Growing Guide</string>
    <string name="tomato_guide_title">🌱 Tomato Growing Guide</string>
    <string name="carrot_guide_title">🌱 Carrot Growing Guide</string>

    <string name="onion_guide">📌 Planting: Plant onion sets or seeds in early spring.\n💧 Water: Keep soil moist but not waterlogged.\n☀️ Light: Full sun (6-8 hours daily).\n🌡️ Temperature: 13-24°C (55-75°F).\n🌱 Soil: Well-draining, fertile soil with compost.\n⏰ Harvest: When tops fall over and turn brown (90-120 days).</string>
    <string name="garlic_guide">📌 Planting: Plant garlic cloves pointy side up in fall.\n💧 Water: Water moderately, keep soil slightly moist.\n☀️ Light: Full sun (6-8 hours daily).\n🌡️ Temperature: 10-25°C (50-77°F).\n🌱 Soil: Loose, well-draining soil rich in organic matter.\n⏰ Harvest: When lower leaves turn brown (8-9 months).</string>
    <string name="cucumber_guide">📌 Planting: Sow seeds directly after frost or start indoors.\n💧 Water: Keep soil consistently moist, water at base.\n☀️ Light: Full sun (6-8 hours daily).\n🌡️ Temperature: 18-29°C (65-85°F).\n🌱 Soil: Rich, well-draining soil with compost.\n⏰ Harvest: When fruits are firm and green (50-70 days).</string>
    <string name="tomato_guide">📌 Planting: Start seeds indoors 6-8 weeks before last frost.\n💧 Water: Water deeply and regularly, avoid wetting leaves.\n☀️ Light: Full sun (6-8 hours daily).\n🌡️ Temperature: 18-27°C (65-80°F).\n🌱 Soil: Rich, well-draining soil with compost.\n⏰ Harvest: When fruits are fully colored and slightly soft (60-85 days).</string>
    <string name="carrot_guide">📌 Planting: Sow seeds directly in loose soil in spring.\n💧 Water: Keep soil consistently moist for germination.\n☀️ Light: Full sun to partial shade.\n🌡️ Temperature: 10-24°C (50-75°F).\n🌱 Soil: Loose, sandy soil free of rocks.\n⏰ Harvest: When tops are 1-2 cm in diameter (60-80 days).</string>

