    <string name="light_dialog_title">Light Threshold Settings</string>
    <string name="light_dialog_short">Set the light level (0–100%) at which the lamp turns on automatically.</string>
    <string name="light_dialog_description">This setting controls automatic lighting. Choose a value below which the plant lacks light.\n\nExample: at 40%, when brightness drops below this level, the LED lamp turns on.\n\n• 0% — Lamp always OFF\n• 100% — Lamp always ON</string>
    <string name="light_dialog_recommendation">📌 How to adjust:\nObserve the daily cycle. Set the threshold so that the lamp supports the plant on cloudy days or extends the day by a few hours in the evening.\n\n💡 Optimal threshold for most houseplants: 40-50%</string>
    <string name="light_dialog_current">💡 Current light level: %d%%</string>

    <string name="soil_dialog_title">Soil Moisture Settings</string>
    <string name="soil_dialog_short">Set the moisture level (0–100%) that triggers watering.</string>
    <string name="soil_dialog_description">Automatic watering activates when soil moisture drops 2% below the set threshold.\n\nThe device waters for 2 minutes, then waits 5 minutes for moisture absorption. If the threshold is still not reached, the cycle repeats until the selected value is achieved.</string>
    <string name="soil_dialog_recommendation">📌 How to adjust (The "Finger Method"):\n\n1. Wait until the soil is dry at a depth of 2-3 cm\n2. Check the reading in the app\n3. Set the threshold 5% higher — this will be the ideal moment to start watering</string>
    <string name="soil_dialog_water_tank">💧 Water tank</string>
    <string name="soil_dialog_watering">🚰 Watering</string>
